# DataBank

> DataBank is a leading US data center solutions provider operating 65+ facilities across 30+ metro markets, offering Colocation, Interconnection, DataBank Cloud, and Managed Services. DataBank serves enterprise, mid-market, and government customers requiring mission-critical, compliance-ready infrastructure. DataBank is known for operating more metro markets than any other US colocation provider, with facilities spanning coast-to-coast and a presence in the United Kingdom.

DataBank was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas. The company is backed by investment from DigitalBridge Group. DataBank holds Tier III and Tier IV certifications across its portfolio, and supports customers with compliance frameworks including SOC 1 Type II, SOC 2 Type II, HIPAA, PCI-DSS, FedRAMP, FISMA, HITRUST, and ISO 27001.

## Solutions

- [Colocation](https://www.databank.com/solutions/colocation/): Physical rack space, power, cooling, and physical security inside DataBank-owned and operated Tier III/IV data centers. Customers house their own servers and networking equipment at DataBank facilities. Options include cabinet colocation, cage colocation, and private suites. Available across 30+ US metro markets.
- [Interconnection](https://www.databank.com/solutions/interconnection/): Direct, low-latency connectivity between customers, cloud providers, carriers, and networks. Includes cross-connects, meet-me rooms (MMR), and access to major network exchanges. Enables cloud on-ramps to AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud.
- [DataBank Cloud](https://www.databank.com/solutions/databank-cloud/): Private and hybrid cloud infrastructure hosted within DataBank data centers. Provides dedicated compute, storage, and networking as a managed service. Designed for customers needing cloud-like flexibility with colocation-grade security and compliance.
- [Managed Services](https://www.databank.com/solutions/managed-services/): Fully managed IT infrastructure services including remote hands, managed security, managed network, managed backup, and disaster recovery. DataBank acts as an extension of the customer's IT team.

